WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.820
<b>Ramen</b>

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:12.800
Would you like a paper apron?

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.070
Yes, thank you.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.940
Hello. My name is Koizumi.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:24.710
I came to this shop to enjoy 
some of my favorite ramen.

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:27.590
The walls are covered 
in beautiful paintings.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.460
The whole place is filled with 
cute red and green objects.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.370
They're drawn on the walls and the lanterns.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.970
Yes, those are...

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:37.180
Thank you for waiting.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.350
<b>Taiyo no Tomato Ramen</b>

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.350
My latest favorite...

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:44.980
Deep red tomato ramen.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:04.500
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:05.040
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:05.960
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:20.990
<b>Tomato Ramen</b>

00:02:22.360 --> 00:02:23.600
Time to eat.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:29.670
The slippery noodles are coated with the 
faintly acidic and sweet taste of tomato.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:33.670
The melted cheese mingles with that.

00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:40.550
This is...

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:46.900
irresistible!

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:52.270
At a restaurant I visited the other day,

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:55.100
they had over ten different 
types of tomato ramen.

00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:58.280
I had trouble deciding which to get.

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:02.780
Since it's gotten hot lately,
the cold noodles also look really good.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:04.530
But still...

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:16.000
Eating piping-hot ramen that makes 
you sweat is simply something else.

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.840
<b>Sigh...</b>

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:26.120
The other pleasure that tomato 
ramen brings with it is this.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:29.140
You take this rice with furikake

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:32.830
and put it into your leftover 
soup to make a sort of risotto.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.790
This is the true charm of this ramen.

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.950
Lycopene, an antioxidant found in tomatoes,

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:43.610
is known to be good for 
clear skin and digestion.

00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:46.620
I don't leave a single molecule of it behind.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.790
Incidentally, lycopene is 
a fat-soluble vitamin.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:54.040
Its absorption rate increases almost 
four times when it's heated in oil.

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.870
<b>Oil</b>

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:51.870
<b>Oil</b>

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:55.380
Here you go.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:57.630
Your tomato juice.

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:03.860
Talking about tomato ramen makes me think 
of the ramen Yuu-san made me that one time.

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:05.720
That was tomato-based, too.

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.430
In France, the tomato is 
called "the apple of love."

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.530
That is to say, the tomato 
is a symbol of love.

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:17.820
I can't deny that ramen was full of love.

00:04:18.380 --> 00:04:22.890
I have trouble being honest about my 
feelings and always act cold toward her,

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:26.820
but the truth is, I want to become 
better friends with Yuu-san.

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:30.450
My feelings are passionate, 
just like this ripe tomato.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.830
Someday, I'll tell her.

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:41.500
Either way, today's ramen 
was delicious again.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.480
What have you been mumbling 
about all this time?

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:47.620
It's annoying.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:50.580
Oh, whoops! You heard me? Starting when?

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.340
Somewhere around "Hello. My name is Koizumi."

00:04:53.340 --> 00:04:56.350
Oh, man, how embarrassing! 
You heard the whole thing!

00:04:56.860 --> 00:05:00.610
So about that restaurant 
you were talking about...

00:05:01.270 --> 00:05:03.570
I don't remember going there with you.

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:05.300
How do you know about that place?

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.610
Oh, really?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.660
Thank you for waiting.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.000
Ah, here it is!

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.520
My turn now.

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:19.190
Time to eat.

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:26.000
Well, it's true that the ramen you 
made for me back then was tasty.

00:05:27.890 --> 00:05:29.600
But that's all.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.930
<b>Whole
Tomatoes</b>

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.930
Thank you for visiting 
Shinjuku Nylord.

00:05:32.110 --> 00:05:33.930
Thank you very much!

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:35.920
Thank you for the food.

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:38.520
What? But I'm not done eating!

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:40.730
Koizumi-san!

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.360
So sad...

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.820
<i>She's acting the same as ever today.</i>

00:05:48.060 --> 00:05:49.870
<i>The faintly acidic and sweet taste...</i>

00:05:51.070 --> 00:05:52.330
<i>So good.</i>

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.320
Excuse me!

00:05:56.320 --> 00:05:58.250
Can I have some ramen risotto, please?

00:06:00.150 --> 00:06:03.980
Maybe I'll travel to Fussa tomorrow.

00:06:06.050 --> 00:06:07.010
<b>Slurp...</b>

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:08.130
Wait!

00:06:08.130 --> 00:06:11.130
Doesn't the red on the Italian 
flag stand for tomatoes?

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:13.700
And the white is for cheese, 
and the green for olives?

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:15.770
Wrong.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.770
<b>Patriotism</b>

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.770
<b>Justice</b>

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:15.770
<b>Homeland</b>

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.770
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.770
<b>Euglena</b>

00:06:22.080 --> 00:06:26.850
As we see here, unicellular organisms can 
be divided into animal and plant types.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:32.280
Amoeba and paramecium are animal types.
Closterium and pinnularia are plant types.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:35.290
Euglena

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:35.290
The green bug, or euglena, is classified 
as being between those groups.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:37.660
It's called a "bug," but it is not an insect.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:40.400
It moves using a tentacle called a flagellum,

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:44.840
but it is also capable of photosynthesis 
and a truly remarkable...

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:44.840
<i>Yesterday, Koizumi-san...</i>

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:49.430
It's true that the ramen you made 
for me back then was tasty.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.050
But that's all.

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.060
<i>Koizumi-san...</i>

00:06:57.010 --> 00:07:01.060
<i>It's okay to be honest and say 
how you really feel, you know.</i>

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:05.070
<i>I'm always ready to accept your feelings.</i>

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:13.300
I'd really like to have some of 
your homemade ramen again,

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.830
but I'm too embarrassed to ask.

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.830
<i>Yes, I love it!</i>

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:19.710
Ouch!

00:07:20.010 --> 00:07:23.070
What are you mumbling about
with that grin on your face?

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:25.420
You'd look scary to anyone who didn't know you.

00:07:25.420 --> 00:07:27.520
Hey, that's mean...

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.470
Huh?

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:31.880
Where is everyone?

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:34.430
Come on, we're leaving.

00:07:34.430 --> 00:07:36.050
Where are you going?

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:41.800
So that's it.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.320
We had cleaning duty.

00:07:43.320 --> 00:07:46.600
Euglena, euglena...

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.230
Hmm, hmm, hmm, 4-1-1-4...

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:50.410
Euglena are great...

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:50.410
What are you singing?

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:52.250
You haven't heard it?

00:07:52.250 --> 00:07:55.150
There's this infomercial about 
euglena that airs late at night.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:57.490
Really? I had no idea.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.600
I've been really into them lately.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:03.960
They say that eating cookies and jellies 
made with it is good for the skin.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:04.900
Really?

00:08:04.900 --> 00:08:06.290
But they're bugs.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:09.090
I thought you hated bugs. 
You're okay with that?

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:12.970
If it's for beauty, I can even 
eat bugs without <i>bug</i>ging out.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:14.750
That was so lame.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.350
Oh, shut up!

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:21.350
<i>We just learned in class that it's 
not a bug, but a type of algae.</i>

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:25.090
<i>The green bug, also known as euglena.</i>

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:27.760
<i>With a scientific name 
meaning "beautiful eye,"</i>

00:08:27.760 --> 00:08:31.520
<i>this single-celled organism has
a length of 0.05 millimeters.</i>

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:34.370
<i>This organism, with over 
60 different nutrients,</i>

00:08:34.370 --> 00:08:36.190
<i>is used in a variety of health foods.</i>

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:39.380
<i>Thanks to its ability to photosynthesize,</i>

00:08:39.380 --> 00:08:41.190
<i>it's also being closely studied</i>

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:45.370
<i>in various fields, such as to mitigate 
global warming or as a bio-fuel.</i>

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:48.470
Euglena, huh?

00:08:48.470 --> 00:08:50.960
<i>I'd like to know what it tastes like.</i>

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.710
<i>N-Not because it's popular now or anything!</i>

00:08:54.710 --> 00:08:57.920
<i>It's just my natural curiosity 
about single-celled organisms.</i>

00:08:57.920 --> 00:09:02.600
<i>I mean, I'm actually considering entering 
a scientific field after graduation.</i>

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.560
Euglena.

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:06.390
Wh-What?

00:09:06.390 --> 00:09:08.100
They use it in ramen, too.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:08.650
Huh?

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:12.480
There's one with about six hundred 
million euglena in the soup.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.220
It's called green ramen.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:19.390
After hearing you talk, I got 
the urge to go have some again.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:20.740
Hey, Koizumi-san...

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:22.420
Do you have a moment?

00:09:22.420 --> 00:09:23.620
Yes?

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:25.980
So that ramen...

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:28.850
This is the place.

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:32.130
<b>Yamate Ramen
Hongo
Anan</b>

00:09:28.850 --> 00:09:30.000
Huh...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.130
Their sign looks like a blackboard.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.600
I don't think it's the reason,

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.180
but apparently students from
Tokyo University often come here to work.

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:39.450
Really?

00:09:44.920 --> 00:09:47.190
I'm splurging today on extra green.

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:49.600
You can add more green, huh?

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.400
Well, anyway...

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:52.850
Time to eat.

00:09:54.370 --> 00:09:59.340
This green color is made by 
hundreds of millions of euglena.

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:15.510
<i>This reminds me of
Italian food made with basil.</i>

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:29.520
<i>Right this moment,</i>

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:38.180
<i>six hundred millions of these 
euglena are flowing into my body.</i>

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:48.830
Thank you for the food.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:51.520
I really liked the basil taste,

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:54.820
but I couldn't really tell what 
the euglena actually tastes like.

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.200
No?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:11:01.170
Then would you like to go to a place where 
they put euglena directly into the noodles?

00:11:01.170 --> 00:11:02.720
What? You mean right now?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:05.020
I don't think I can go right now.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.530
I'm too full.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:10.390
It's a short train ride, or we could 
go by foot and walk some of this off.

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:15.040
Is it really a good idea to consume 
that much euglena in one day?

00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:18.490
I ended up eating another bowl.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.490
<b>Oof...
So full...</b>

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:21.060
Is this another property of euglena?

00:11:20.400 --> 00:11:23.320
<b>Hi!</b>

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:23.550
No, I think it's a property of Koizumi-san.

00:11:23.550 --> 00:11:25.990
I'm going to the next shop now.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:31.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:36.020
<b>Huge Line</b>

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:36.500
<i>Take a look at this huge line!</i>

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:39.190
<i>Today we're visiting a popular 
sweets shop that has</i>

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:42.630
<b>The Miraculous Line for Sweets!</b>

00:11:39.190 --> 00:11:41.380
<i>a line going around the block every day!</i>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:44.130
<i>Let's see what these people 
have to say about it.</i>

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:45.540
Wow, that's crazy.

00:11:45.540 --> 00:11:48.060
<i>I stood in line for three hours to get these.</i>

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:50.830
<i>I can brag at school tomorrow!</i>

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:51.770
Whoa...

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.720
Is it really good enough 
to be worth all that?

00:11:55.390 --> 00:11:59.280
I bet you stand in line for 
ramen shops pretty often, right?

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:03.530
I don't really like standing 
in line, to be honest.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.320
I avoid it whenever I can.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:08.730
Oh, really? That's unexpected.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.790
<i>I would've thought she'd happily 
stand in line for ramen.</i>

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:17.960
<i>I guess she must know a bunch of places 
where you don't have to stand in line.</i>

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:20.720
<i>Yeah, that must be it.</i>

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:26.070
<i>There's no reason why she would 
ever have to stand in line.</i>

00:12:35.900 --> 00:12:38.730
<b>Mutekiya Ramen</b>

00:12:41.360 --> 00:12:43.630
About another hour, you think?

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:44.620
Yeah.

00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:45.190
Man, it's hot.

00:12:44.620 --> 00:12:46.650
Yeah, I'm already in line.

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:47.460
Looks like we'll move up soon.

00:12:46.650 --> 00:12:48.170
It's crazy long.

00:12:47.460 --> 00:12:48.960
We've been here a long time.

00:12:49.870 --> 00:12:51.140
It's so hot.

00:12:51.140 --> 00:12:52.860
<i>An hour down.</i>

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:55.260
<i>Standing in line in the summer is brutal.</i>

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:57.880
<i>But I have to do this!</i>

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:03.630
Today, I'm
going to
this place

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:03.630
<i>Koizumi-san was totally reading 
up on this place today.</i>

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:00.630
<b>Appear</b>

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:00.500
<b>Peek</b>

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:06.890
<i>I'm positive that she's fixated 
on Mutekiya right now.</i>

00:13:07.450 --> 00:13:10.390
<i>But Koizumi-san's got class duty this week.</i>

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.390
<i>Hey, cute girl over there</i>

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.240
<i>That's why I went to stand in line for her.</i>

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:18.650
<i>Enjoy your ramen</i>

00:13:15.240 --> 00:13:19.340
<i>Once she gets here, I'll give her my 
spot and smoothly make my exit.</i>

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:19.900
<i>Ba-dump</i>

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:22.650
<i>I have to say, great idea, me!</i>

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:26.940
<i>My very own "if pressure 
doesn't work, try leaving" plan!</i>

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.740
Hello? Where are you?

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.410
What? You're gonna be a bit longer?

00:13:28.690 --> 00:13:33.040
<i>Still, I thought she said she 
doesn't like to stand in line.</i>

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.810
<i>She just couldn't admit it.</i>

00:13:35.800 --> 00:13:37.470
<i>That's cute in its own way.</i>

00:13:37.470 --> 00:13:39.820
All right, please step forward.

00:13:42.340 --> 00:13:46.800
<b>Mutekiya</b>

00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:45.950
<i>Finally, I'm on the side where the store is!</i>

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.120
Hurry up!

00:13:47.120 --> 00:13:48.470
Where the hell are you?

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:50.160
Please take a look while you wait.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.720
Okay!

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:53.520
Thank you very much.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.890
<i>This store has tonkotsu base, my favorite.</i>

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.700
This looks so good!

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.200
Oh, you're close? Where?

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:02.030
<i>I should come here to eat it myself sometime.</i>

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.850
Oh, I see you.

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.000
Over here!

00:14:04.400 --> 00:14:06.400
You guys are so late.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.660
Yeah, sorry.

00:14:07.660 --> 00:14:10.560
It was too hot, so we took 
a break at a Starbucks.

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:13.300
Heya! I see you're almost at the front.

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:15.790
Hey, girlie.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:18.520
<b>Crowd</b>

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:19.780
Can you step back a bit? 
My friends need to get in here.

00:14:19.780 --> 00:14:21.000
E-Excuse me?!

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.000
<b>WHAT</b>

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.000
<i>This is cutting!</i>

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:28.000
E-Excuse me, but I don't think cutting is right.

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:30.970
Huh? But I've been standing 
here for them the whole time.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:34.350
I've been standing here for 
almost an hour in this heat.

00:14:34.350 --> 00:14:36.160
It was hard, let me tell you.

00:14:36.160 --> 00:14:38.690
Uh, hang on! The same goes for me!

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:41.760
In fact, everyone here has 
been standing just as long!

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:43.320
She's right.

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:44.630
Come on...

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:47.500
Let it slide just this once, okay?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:48.940
I don't normally do this.

00:14:50.400 --> 00:14:53.530
<i>This guy is messing things up 
for everyone, and he knows it!</i>

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.440
Is that girl alone?

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:57.430
I guess she doesn't have 
anyone to eat with.

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:58.460
Kinda sad.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:02.130
Th-Th-This isn't something you 
normally eat in a group!

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:04.130
And anyway, that's not even the point!

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.940
What are you doing?

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:17.220
Koizumi-san! Can you believe this?!

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:20.480
I don't know why you're here,

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.610
but you're making a scene 
in front of this restaurant.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:26.860
I'm here to stand in line for you.

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:30.200
I wanted you to be able 
to just walk right in.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:32.990
Cutting in line is also a disturbance.

00:15:32.990 --> 00:15:35.280
I know that!

00:15:35.280 --> 00:15:39.160
I was going to give you my spot and go home!

00:15:39.160 --> 00:15:40.370
Wait, what?

00:15:40.370 --> 00:15:41.770
Oh, so that girl's a gopher.

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:42.980
I'm not!

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:45.010
This was an act of innocent love!

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:46.500
Anyway...

00:15:46.940 --> 00:15:52.450
It seems there are quite a number of people 
who think nothing of cutting in line,

00:15:52.450 --> 00:15:55.510
and it's bound to happen at 
any restaurant with huge lines.

00:15:55.900 --> 00:16:00.920
I guess. I mean, there are people who will 
do it even after you point it out to them.

00:16:02.700 --> 00:16:04.550
What are you talking about?

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:07.420
A real ramen lover would never do that.

00:16:07.420 --> 00:16:09.780
Obviously, there are <i>some</i> who would.

00:16:09.780 --> 00:16:12.030
I don't know if they're 
real ramen lovers, though.

00:16:13.020 --> 00:16:17.890
Only so many bowls of ramen can be crafted 
by the people who work in this store.

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:24.540
This store also has a person who prepares the 
soup for the next day instead of sleeping.

00:16:24.840 --> 00:16:30.300
Stealing even one bowl of that soup from 
its rightful owner in line is something

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:33.510
a true ramen lover would never do.

00:16:35.570 --> 00:16:36.770
Never ever.

00:16:42.050 --> 00:16:45.020
I'll get in line and wait myself.

00:16:45.590 --> 00:16:50.060
Seeing the line order change would 
confuse the people working here.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:53.460
Then I'll get in line again, too!

00:16:53.460 --> 00:16:55.580
Do as you like, I guess.

00:16:55.580 --> 00:16:56.780
Yes!

00:16:57.210 --> 00:16:59.410
Wait up, Koizumi-san!

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:06.880
Anyway, the shop's staff was really nice...

00:17:08.540 --> 00:17:10.900
So you're standing back here now, too?

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:17.140
Well, you might not think it, 
but we do love ramen quite a bit.

00:17:18.520 --> 00:17:19.630
I see!

00:17:21.110 --> 00:17:24.690
I don't know, but I'd say this all 
turned out okay. Right, Koizumi-san?

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:26.090
What are you talking about?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:27.690
<b>Move This Way</b>

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:30.440
<b>Please do not queue beyond this point.
Instead, please queue on the other side of the street.</b>

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.440
Still, I was pretty surprised.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:31.160
Huh?

00:17:31.160 --> 00:17:35.200
The other day, you said you don't 
really like waiting in line.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:37.680
I don't like waiting in line,

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:42.720
but I also know that if you wait a
little longer, the line won't be as bad.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.200
But then, why...

00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:51.380
Because I was taken over by impulse.

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:55.670
I just had to have this store's ramen at once.

00:17:56.500 --> 00:18:00.680
Once you're in that place,
you have no choice but to line up.

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:05.910
An impulse... Is the ramen here really that good?

00:18:05.910 --> 00:18:07.650
I like it.

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:08.810
I see.

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.460
Let's take a picture with the huge line!

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:12.770
A memento of this trip!

00:18:13.030 --> 00:18:16.230
I've started a food blog 
for places with huge lines.

00:18:16.230 --> 00:18:17.150
Really?

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:20.030
Yeah, I've been standing 
here for two hours now.

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:22.620
Nah, it's not that impressive!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:25.270
I guess there are people here specifically 
because they want to stand in line.

00:18:26.040 --> 00:18:28.160
That can be its own entertainment.

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:33.670
<b>Mutekiya Ramen</b>

00:18:28.570 --> 00:18:30.940
It's its own good fortune, in a way.

00:18:31.520 --> 00:18:33.670
I guess so.

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:35.920
<b>Mutekiya</b>

00:18:34.320 --> 00:18:35.920
Thank you for waiting!

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.550
We... We can finally eat!

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:41.600
The wait was worth it!

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.760
Time to eat.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:45.100
This looks so good.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:56.570
<i>It's delicious!</i>

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:00.380
<i>The rich tonkotsu soup 
clings to the thick noodles!</i>

00:19:05.560 --> 00:19:07.060
<i>And free toppings!</i>

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:09.620
<i>Garlic! Pickled mustard greens! Fish powder!</i>

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:11.620
<i>I'll switch it up with some 
pickled mustard greens!</i>

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:21.090
<i>This is bliss.</i>

00:19:21.620 --> 00:19:26.100
<i>It's like this soup is melting away 
the exhaustion of that long wait.</i>

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:36.960
<i>I'm seriously getting hooked.</i>

00:19:39.570 --> 00:19:42.200
<b>Mutekiya Ramen</b>

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.200
That was amazing.

00:19:42.200 --> 00:19:46.200
<b>Mutekiya Ramen</b>

00:19:46.820 --> 00:19:48.640
<i>Bliss...</i>

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.980
Hey, Koizumi-san!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.500
Let's stand in line for that ramen again!

00:19:54.170 --> 00:19:56.500
<b>Yuu is hooked
on the ramen
and the line</b>

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:00.480
Why don't you go by yourself?

00:20:00.480 --> 00:20:05.940
Standing alone for two hours is not at 
all like standing with you for two hours!

00:20:05.940 --> 00:20:10.390
Do you remember what you're not 
supposed to do while standing in line?

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.240
Yes!

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:15.350
Don't be loud in front of the restaurant, 
and don't cut in line.

00:20:15.350 --> 00:20:20.280
On top of that, stalking me 
is also against the rules.

00:20:24.380 --> 00:20:31.320
I-I need to watch over her so that 
nobody does something like that to her!

00:20:31.320 --> 00:20:35.000
Wait! Koizumi-san!

00:20:37.500 --> 00:20:40.000
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Morning Ramen</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Hiyashi</b>

00:22:09.970 --> 00:22:29.990
<b>Museum</b>

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:14.950
Things that happen with ramen!

00:22:14.950 --> 00:22:16.910
Getting a big portion because 
it's free, but it's gross!

00:22:16.910 --> 00:22:17.960
I've been there!

00:22:17.960 --> 00:22:19.520
Do I use black pepper or shichimi?

00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:20.580
I've been there!

00:22:20.580 --> 00:22:22.330
Can't get chopsticks out of the dispenser.

00:22:22.330 --> 00:22:23.320
I've been there!

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:26.380
When ordering fish-based broths, do I pick 
a sardine, mackerel, or flying fish base?

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:29.080
Not... sure if I've been there?

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:36.000
<b>Thank you for the food!</b>
